==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s (1,800%) spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 12 seconds<sup>360f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Pigge]]s spawn after 21.33 seconds<sup>640f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Large Iron Ball]] spawns.
**6 [[Large Red Ball]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**8 [[Large White Ball]]s spawn, delay 5~6.67 seconds<sup>150f~200f</sup>.
**7 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 5~6.67 seconds<sup>150f~200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
All you really need to do to beat this level is spam midrangers with Area Attack such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]. Using a [[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critter]] such as [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] to make taking down the Iron Ball quicker is recommended too. Meatshields and other Melee Cats are generally a bad idea here, since they will only act as a stepping stone for the enemies.

